  "$id": "https://lifegames.org/schemas/copy.app.schema.json",
  "title": "LifegamesCopyApp",
  "description": "Rich authoring schema for the app slice of @lifegames/copy. Every customer-facing UI string in the iOS/watchOS LifePortal app — navigation titles, tab labels, section headers, buttons, alerts, field labels, placeholders, and interpolated templates — is a CopyString leaf carrying authoring context in _meta. Source of truth is ios-LifegamesPortal/LifePortal/Packages/LifePortalFeatures/Sources/** (verified file:line in each leaf's _meta.usage). The copy build derives a FLAT schema from this one (stripping _meta) for all consumer codegen (TS/Zod/Swift). Strings are authored in ICU MessageFormat 1 syntax; interpolated templates carry their ICU placeholders ({count}, {percent}, {relative}, …) and ICU plural syntax where the source pluralizes — consumers keep their native plural logic. Stored in natural case: the app uppercases section headers / buttons at the call site via .textCase / .kerning, so stored values are natural case ('Sync Now', not 'SYNC NOW'). Every object group has a UNIQUE title (App* / Perm-free App-prefixed) so quicktype-derived Swift struct names never collide across namespaces. The $defs block is byte-identical to schema/identity.schema.json, schema/widgets.schema.json, and schema/a11y.schema.json; the $defs are inlined per schema file (no cross-file $ref), which the flat-schema derivation requires.",
